=== TITLE: USG Left Hemithorax / Chest (Left) ===
=== IMPRESSION ===
NORMAL LEFT THORACIC ULTRASOUND STUDY.
- No pleural effusion, subpleural consolidation, or pneumothorax in left hemithorax.

=== FINDINGS ===
STUDY: HIGH-RESOLUTION THORACIC ULTRASONOGRAPHY (LEFT HEMITHORAX)

OBSERVATIONS:
- LEFT PLEURAL LINE: Smooth, thin, and continuous with preserved lung sliding motion.
- LEFT PLEURAL CAVITY: Clear costophrenic and cardiophrenic recesses without free or loculated pleural effusion.
- LEFT LUNG: Normal aeration pattern. No consolidation, atelectasis, or mass lesion.
- LEFT HEMIDIAPHRAGM: Normal position, contour, and respiratory excursion.